   "l": "Good travelling — no ruts, no tracks;",
   "v": true,
   "n": "Five sayings follow, all built alike: 善 + a craft + 無 + the very tool or trace that craft is supposed to leave. 善行 is 'good travelling', not 'a good traveller' — there is no man in the Chinese at all, and English has to resist supplying one. Wang Bi's gloss opens all five: go along with what is so of itself, contrive nothing and add nothing, and there is nothing left over to show.",
