   "n": "數 is a three-way polyphone: here it is shǔ, 'to count'; in chapter 5's 多言數窮 it was shuò, 'again and again'; and it turns up once more in chapter 39. 籌策 are the physical rods a Warring States accountant laid out — the calculating machine of the age. The compound later came to mean 'to plan, to scheme', which is how the line is usually felt: the good reckoner has no need to calculate."
