   "l": "Therefore the sage is abidingly good at saving men,\nand so there are no thrown-away men;",
   "v": true,
   "i": "So the sage is always good at rescuing people, and no one is left to be thrown away;",
   "n": "常 is chapter 1's 'abiding', here doing adverbial duty with nothing to mark it. 無棄人 is the verb 棄 with its object 人 standing as a whole after 無, and it can be taken two ways with nothing on the page to decide: 'he discards no one', or 'there are no discarded men'. We print the second, which is how Wang Bi's 故無棄人也 closes his comment; the first is not shut out."
